<item>
            <title>[LU-20941] tests: conf-sanity reformat fails on dm-flakey devices left by an earlier run</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20941</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;conf-sanity fails every test at its first reformat, before any subtest runs, when the dm-flakey devices of an earlier run on the same nodes are still in place:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Formatting mgs, mds, osts
Format mds1: /dev/vdb
co5-mds: mkfs.lustre FATAL: Unable to build fs /dev/vdb (256)
co5-mds: mkfs.lustre FATAL: mkfs failed 256
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;dmsetup ls&lt;/tt&gt; on the MDS still shows &lt;tt&gt;mds1_flakey&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;mds2_flakey&lt;/tt&gt; as linear maps over /dev/vdb and /dev/vdc, with nothing mounted, so mkfs on the raw disk fails.  Removing them by hand (&lt;tt&gt;dmsetup remove&lt;/tt&gt;) lets the run proceed.  Seen on master (2.17.59) with an ltvm 3-node cluster (separate MDS, OSS, client, real block devices, no failover hosts), running conf-sanity twice in a row, or after llmount.sh, without llmountcleanup.sh in between.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Cause&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;stop()&lt;/tt&gt; only calls &lt;tt&gt;dm_cleanup_dev()&lt;/tt&gt; when the facet has a distinct failover host, &lt;tt&gt;CLEANUP_DM_DEV&lt;/tt&gt; is true, or the facet is &lt;tt&gt;fs*&lt;/tt&gt;.  &lt;tt&gt;init_test_env&lt;/tt&gt; sets &lt;tt&gt;CLEANUP_DM_DEV=false&lt;/tt&gt;, so in a non-failover setup the mapper normally outlives &lt;tt&gt;stop()&lt;/tt&gt; and is reused by the next &lt;tt&gt;mount_facet()&lt;/tt&gt;, which is intended.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;check_and_setup_lustre()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;setupall()&lt;/tt&gt; reformat with &lt;tt&gt;CLEANUP_DM_DEV=true formatall&lt;/tt&gt;, which removes those mappers first.  But &lt;tt&gt;reformat()&lt;/tt&gt; in conf-sanity-framework.sh calls plain &lt;tt&gt;formatall&lt;/tt&gt;, so a conf-sanity started on nodes where a previous run (any suite, or llmount.sh) left its mappers runs mkfs on the raw device underneath them.  A new test process also starts with &lt;tt&gt;${facet}_dev&lt;/tt&gt; pointing at the raw device, so it never learns that the mapper exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10893&quot; title=&quot;all conf-sanity tests failed: format mgs: mkfs.lustre FATAL: Unable to build fs&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-10893&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10893&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fixed the same mkfs failure in 2018; this path still bypasses it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Related%3Admcleanupdev%28%29leavesthefacetdeviceexportedwhenthemapperisgone&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Related: dm_cleanup_dev() leaves the facet device exported when the mapper is gone&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;dm_cleanup_dev() {
	...
	is_dm_dev $facet $dm_dev || &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; 0
	...
	unexport_dm_dev $facet
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the mapper was already removed (by another process, or by a &lt;tt&gt;stop()&lt;/tt&gt; in a subshell, whose &lt;tt&gt;unexport_dm_dev()&lt;/tt&gt; only changes that subshell), &lt;tt&gt;dm_cleanup_dev()&lt;/tt&gt; returns before &lt;tt&gt;unexport_dm_dev()&lt;/tt&gt;, so &lt;tt&gt;${facet}_dev&lt;/tt&gt; keeps the /dev/mapper path and the next start mounts a device that no longer exists.  With &lt;tt&gt;CLEANUP_DM_DEV=true&lt;/tt&gt; set in cfg/local.sh, ltvm saw sanity test_160h and test_278 fail this way on every run (ltvm commit b8d9abd121b1).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Suggestedfix&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Suggested fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;conf-sanity-framework.sh &lt;tt&gt;reformat()&lt;/tt&gt;: &lt;tt&gt;CLEANUP_DM_DEV=true formatall&lt;/tt&gt;, as &lt;tt&gt;check_and_setup_lustre()&lt;/tt&gt; does, or have &lt;tt&gt;formatall()&lt;/tt&gt; remove any existing &lt;tt&gt;${facet}_flakey&lt;/tt&gt; map of the facets it formats before running mkfs.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;dm_cleanup_dev()&lt;/tt&gt;: call &lt;tt&gt;unexport_dm_dev()&lt;/tt&gt; also when &lt;tt&gt;is_dm_dev&lt;/tt&gt; finds no mapper.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Workaround: run llmountcleanup.sh (cleanupall, which uses &lt;tt&gt;CLEANUP_DM_DEV=true&lt;/tt&gt;) before starting conf-sanity, as ltvm&apos;s &lt;tt&gt;suite run&lt;/tt&gt; does.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
